      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "WebDyne versions from 3.007 before 3.022 for Perl execute .psp files outside the document root via path traversal in the PSGI API route fallback.\n\nWhen a request matches no file, the PSGI handler retries it as an API route through api_filename. That keeps .. segments in the request path and only checks that the joined path starts with the document root, which a request for /../private passes.\n\nA remote attacker can run the embedded Perl in any .psp file the server can read, such as one uploaded to a directory outside the document root.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
